\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3.1}{\ignorespaces Class distribution across the three MedMNIST datasets. (a) PathMNIST exhibits extreme imbalance (195:1), dominated by nuclei and background tissue. (b) ChestMNIST label prevalences vary by over 30$\times $, with Infiltration the most common and Hernia the rarest. (c) DermaMNIST is dominated by Melanocytic Nevus at 49.6\%, with Vascular Lesion and Dermatofibroma collectively representing under 6\% of samples.}}{19}{figure.caption.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:dataset_overview}{{3.1}{19}{Class distribution across the three MedMNIST datasets. (a) PathMNIST exhibits extreme imbalance (195:1), dominated by nuclei and background tissue. (b) ChestMNIST label prevalences vary by over 30$\times $, with Infiltration the most common and Hernia the rarest. (c) DermaMNIST is dominated by Melanocytic Nevus at 49.6\%, with Vascular Lesion and Dermatofibroma collectively representing under 6\% of samples}{figure.caption.2}{}}
